From 01eaefcaf5cd7ce715fd8759b3b4bc23b0d2d2f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Nov 2023 15:06:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 096/149] mtk: hostapd: add support for DFS channel switching
 with csa sent

Upstream hostapd handles a chan_switch control command to a DFS
channel with a restart of the interface and a CAC, and every client
disconnects. This patch announces the switch with a CSA instead, and
the kernel runs the CAC after the countdown. During that CAC the AP
stays enabled, but it ignores beacon updates and management frames.

A target in non-occupancy fails the command, and so does a width
that the HT, VHT and HE flags do not carry. With the background
chain, the AP waits on an available temporary channel while the chain
runs the CAC of the target. hostapd drops its record of the chain
when an accepted CSA overlaps an idle chain, and after a failed chain
start other than -EBUSY. A failed chain start fails the command only
when the AP waits on a temporary channel. During a CAC on the
operating channel, the command restarts the interface on the
requested channel, also on an ACS radio. If no BSS accepts the CSA,
no chain CAC starts, as in
mtk-openwrt-feeds 6e4012670571 ("[openwrt-24][MAC80211][WiFi7]
[kernel 6.6][Prepare for Filogic 880/860/850 20250905 MP4.2
Release]").

Signed-off-by: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Co-developed-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
